From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lgg <lgg@ubuntu>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: make FDB delete idempotent

During bridge setup and master changes DSA can ask qca8k to delete an
FDB entry that has already been removed from the hardware table. Treat
this as success instead of returning -EINVAL, matching the expected
idempotent semantics of deleting a non-existing FDB entry.

This avoids spurious startup errors such as:

  port 1 failed to delete xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx vid 1 from fdb: -22

on multi-CPU-port qca8k devices while bridge ports are moving between
standalone and bridged state.

Signed-off-by: lgg <lgg@ubuntu>
---
 drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-common.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-common.c
@@ -294,9 +294,9 @@ static int qca8k_fdb_search_and_del(stru
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto exit;
 
-	/* Rule doesn't exist. Why delete? */
+	/* Deleting a non-existing rule is harmless. */
 	if (!fdb.aging) {
-		ret = -EINVAL;
+		ret = 0;
 		goto exit;
 	}
 
